---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "../config/site.config";
// Source: spec/reviewcatcher-legal-pages.md ("Privacy Policy" section).
// Strong draft — for solicitor review before final use; not legal advice.
---

<Layout title={`Privacy Policy | ${siteConfig.name}`} description={`${siteConfig.name} privacy policy.`}>
  <main class="page-shell">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="meta">Last updated: {siteConfig.legal.pagesLastUpdated}</p>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        This policy explains how {siteConfig.name} ("we", "us") handles personal data. It covers
        two different situations, because our role changes depending on whose data it is.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        {siteConfig.name} is a business registered in Ireland ({siteConfig.legal.registrationStatus}),
        based in {siteConfig.contact.address}. For questions about this policy or your data,
        contact us at <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contact.email}`}>{siteConfig.contact.email}</a>
        {siteConfig.contact.phone && <> or {siteConfig.contact.phone}</>}.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Two roles — please read this part</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>When you contact us or use this website</strong> (you're a business owner, a
          lead, or a site visitor), we are the <strong>data controller</strong> — we decide how
          your data is used, and this policy applies to you directly.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>When we send review requests to a client's customers</strong>, we are only the{" "}
          <strong>data processor</strong> — the business that hired us is the controller of that
          data. If you received a review request or reminder text and want your details removed,
          reply STOP to the message or contact the business that serves you; you can also contact
          us and we'll act on their instructions. See our <a href="/dpa">Data Processing Agreement</a>{" "}
          for how we protect that data.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. What we collect (as controller)</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Enquiry / contact data:</strong> name, business name, email, phone number and anything you tell us when you contact us or book a call.</li>
        <li><strong>Client data:</strong> the information needed to provide and bill for the service.</li>
        <li><strong>Website data:</strong> basic analytics (pages visited, approximate location, device/browser) and any cookies you accept — see the cookie note below.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Why we use it, and our legal basis</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To respond to your enquiry and provide the service — <em>performance of a contract</em> / <em>steps prior to a contract</em>.</li>
        <li>To send you service-related messages and, where permitted, occasional updates about {siteConfig.name} — <em>legitimate interests</em> or <em>consent</em>, with an opt-out in every message.</li>
        <li>To meet tax and legal obligations — <em>legal obligation</em>.</li>
        <li>To understand and improve our website — <em>consent</em> (analytics cookies) or <em>legitimate interests</em>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        We use only essential cookies by default. Any analytics or non-essential cookies load
        only if you accept them via our cookie banner. You can withdraw consent at any time in
        your browser settings.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Who we share data with</h2>
      <p>
        We use a small number of trusted service providers ("processors") to run the service —
        for example website hosting, email, SMS delivery and scheduling/automation tools. We
        share only what's needed, under contract, and never sell your data. A current list is
        available on request. Some providers may process data outside the EEA; where they do, we
        rely on appropriate safeguards (such as an adequacy decision or Standard Contractual
        Clauses).
      </p>

      <h2>7. How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        We keep enquiry and client data only as long as needed for the purpose it was collected
        and to meet legal/tax obligations, then delete it. Data we process on behalf of a client
        is kept only for the life of that engagement and deleted or returned when it ends.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You have the right to access, correct, delete, restrict or object to the processing of
        your personal data, to data portability, and to withdraw consent at any time. To exercise
        any of these, contact us at <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contact.email}`}>{siteConfig.contact.email}</a>.
        You also have the right to complain to the Data Protection Commission
        (<strong>dataprotection.ie</strong>).
      </p>

      <h2>9. Changes</h2>
      <p>We may update this policy; the "last updated" date shows the latest version.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
